  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes typecheck. I couldn't run `vite build` or open the page, so how it looks in a browser is untested. The scene draws into the existing #app canvas. A translucent sphere uses a custom GLSL `material.custom` shader with a cyan fresnel rim and horizontal scanlines. The scanlines scroll upward through a `clk` uniform, which is updated every frame via `setUniform`. A small metallic cube rotates inside the sphere. The background is dark, and the floor is a glossy dark PBR plane lit by a cyan point light. A faint additive radial glow with a ring sits on the floor under the sphere. The camera is a perspective camera framing the sphere. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set to true in a `requestAnimationFrame` callback after `app.ready()` resolves.",
